-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART III -- regulations 29 to 34.1: EMPLOYMENT THAT AN
-- EMPLOYEE ELECTS TO BRING IN (sections 29 to 33), employment of an Indian (29.1), placement agencies (34) and
-- employment under an international social security agreement (34.1). Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- Sections 10, 13(3) and 38 of the Act, and paragraphs 6(2)(a), (b), (e), (j), (j.1) and (k) and 15(1)(b) of
-- the Act, belong to piece cp1 or cp2; section 107 of the Act (agreements) belongs to piece cp6. What each decides
-- for the person is a plain input here (-- out of range: sections 6, 10, 13, 15, 38, 107).

§ `Regulations, Part III -- regulations 29 to 34.1`

§§ `Regulation 29(c) to (f): the requirements the employee must meet`

-- 29 ... of an employee in a year who (c) is resident in Canada in the year for the purposes of the Income Tax Act;
-- (d) is not, in respect of that employment, in pensionable employment by virtue of any other provision of the Act
-- or these Regulations; (e) elects in accordance with subsection 13(3) of the Act for the purposes of section 10
-- thereof; and (f) pays the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act within one year after April 30 of
-- the following year or within one year after the day on which an amount is refunded to the employee under section
-- 38 of the Act. The April 30 window is a deadline (a payment before April 30 is in time); the refund window opens
-- on the refund day, which cannot be paid "within a year after" before it happens (fork F15).
-- src:358 | 29 Pensionable employment includes employment in Canada that is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of
-- src:359 | (a) section 28, or
-- src:360 | (b) paragraph 6(2)(a), 6(2)(b) or 6(2)(j) of the Act
-- src:361 | of an employee in a year who
-- src:362 | (c) is resident in Canada in the year for the purposes of the Income Tax Act;
-- src:363 | (d) is not, in respect of that employment, in pensionable employment by virtue of any other provision of the Act or these Regulations;
-- src:364 | (e) elects in accordance with subsection 13(3) of the Act for the purposes of section 10 thereof; and
-- src:365 | (f) pays the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act within one year after April 30 of the following year or within one year after the day on which an amount is refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act.
@ref Reg 29(f) (src:358-365)
GIVEN `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` IS A DATE
      `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(f) — the employee has paid within one year after the day an amount was refunded` `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST refunded THEN `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` refunded (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)

@ref Reg 29(f) (src:358-365)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` IS A DATE
      `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(f) — the employee has paid the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act in time` year `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act` MEANS
        `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid`
        AT MOST (`the date a time limit ends` (YMD (year PLUS 1) 4 30) (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1))
    OR  `reg 29(f) — the employee has paid within one year after the day an amount was refunded` `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act`

@ref Reg 29(c), 29(d), 29(e), 29(f) (src:358-365)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the employee is resident in Canada in the year for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is not pensionable employment by virtue of any other provision of the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee elects in accordance with subsection 13(3) of the Act for the purposes of section 10 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` IS A DATE
      `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(c) to (f) — the employee complies with the requirements` year `the employee is resident in Canada in the year for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` `the employment is not pensionable employment by virtue of any other provision of the Act or these Regulations` `the employee elects in accordance with subsection 13(3) of the Act for the purposes of section 10 of the Act` `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act` MEANS
        `the employee is resident in Canada in the year for the purposes of the Income Tax Act`
    AND `the employment is not pensionable employment by virtue of any other provision of the Act or these Regulations`
    AND `the employee elects in accordance with subsection 13(3) of the Act for the purposes of section 10 of the Act`
    AND `reg 29(f) — the employee has paid the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act in time` year `the day the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act were paid` `the day an amount was refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act`

§§ `Regulations 29 to 33: the employment an employee elects to bring in`

-- 29 Pensionable employment includes employment in Canada that is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of
-- (a) section 28, or (b) paragraph 6(2)(a), 6(2)(b) or 6(2)(j) of the Act, of an employee in a year who meets (c) to (f).
-- src:358 | 29 Pensionable employment includes employment in Canada that is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of
-- src:359 | (a) section 28, or
-- src:360 | (b) paragraph 6(2)(a), 6(2)(b) or 6(2)(j) of the Act
-- src:361 | of an employee in a year who
-- src:362 | (c) is resident in Canada in the year for the purposes of the Income Tax Act;
-- src:363 | (d) is not, in respect of that employment, in pensionable employment by virtue of any other provision of the Act or these Regulations;
-- src:364 | (e) elects in accordance with subsection 13(3) of the Act for the purposes of section 10 thereof; and
-- src:365 | (f) pays the contributions referred to in section 10 of the Act within one year after April 30 of the following year or within one year after the day on which an amount is refunded to the employee under section 38 of the Act.
@ref Reg 29 (src:358-365)
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of section 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of paragraph 6(2)(a), 6(2)(b) or 6(2)(j) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29 — pensionable employment includes the employment in Canada excepted by section 28 or the Act` `the employment is in Canada` `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of section 28` `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of paragraph 6(2)(a), 6(2)(b) or 6(2)(j) of the Act` `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` MEANS
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND (    `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of section 28`
         OR  `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of paragraph 6(2)(a), 6(2)(b) or 6(2)(j) of the Act`)
    AND `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)`

-- 30 Pensionable employment includes employment in Canada, that is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue
-- of subsection 22(1), of an employee in a year by an employer who (a) is not resident in Canada, and (b) does not
-- have an establishment in Canada, if the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f).
