      `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 22(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 30 — pensionable employment includes the employment in Canada excepted by subsection 22(1)` `the employment is in Canada` `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 22(1)` `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` MEANS
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 22(1)`
    AND `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)`

-- 31 Pensionable employment includes employment in international transportation, that is excepted from
-- pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 17(2), of an employee in a year if the employee complies with
-- the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f) and is not required in respect of that employment to contribute to
-- a similar plan under the laws of a country other than Canada.
