GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31 — pensionable employment includes the employment in international transportation excepted by subsection 17(2)` `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 17(2)` `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` `the employee is required in respect of that employment to contribute to a similar plan under the laws of a country other than Canada` MEANS
        `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment by virtue of subsection 17(2)`
    AND `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)`
    AND (NOT `the employee is required in respect of that employment to contribute to a similar plan under the laws of a country other than Canada`)

-- 32 Pensionable employment includes employment outside Canada in a year that would be pensionable employment if it
-- were in Canada in the year, of an employee if the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c)
-- to (f) and is not required in respect of that employment to contribute to a similar plan under the laws of the
-- country in which the employee is employed.
