GIVEN `the employment is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is required in respect of that employment to contribute to a similar plan under the laws of the country in which the employee is employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 32 — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada that would be pensionable in Canada` `the employment is outside Canada` `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada in the year` `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` `the employee is required in respect of that employment to contribute to a similar plan under the laws of the country in which the employee is employed` MEANS
        `the employment is outside Canada`
    AND `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada in the year`
    AND `the employee complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)`
    AND (NOT `the employee is required in respect of that employment to contribute to a similar plan under the laws of the country in which the employee is employed`)

-- 33 For greater certainty, where the employment of an employee is, by virtue of the employee's compliance with the
-- requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f), included in a pensionable employment under any of sections 29 to 32,
-- the employer of that employee is not required to pay an employer's contribution in respect of the employment.
-- (It follows from regulation 7 as well: no employee's contribution is required to be deducted, so the employer's
-- contribution, which equals it, is nil. The tests assert that.)
-- src:380 | 33 For greater certainty, where the employment of an employee is, by virtue of the employee’s compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f) included in a pensionable employment under any of sections 29 to 32, the employer of that employee is not required to pay an employer’s contribution in respect of the employment.
@ref Reg 33 (src:380)
GIVEN `the employment is included in pensionable employment under section 29, 30, 31 or 32 by virtue of the employee's compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 33 — the employer is not required to pay an employer's contribution` `the employment is included in pensionable employment under section 29, 30, 31 or 32 by virtue of the employee's compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)` MEANS
    `the employment is included in pensionable employment under section 29, 30, 31 or 32 by virtue of the employee's compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f)`

§§ `Regulation 29.1: employment of an Indian`

-- 29.1 (1)(b) the employer elects, by completing the form authorized by the Minister, that from the date of filing
-- the form with the Minister or such later date as the employer specifies in the form, the employment of each
-- Indian employee of the employer whose employment is not excepted by other than paragraph 6(2)(j.1) is pensionable
-- employment. The election takes effect on the day of filing, or on the specified day if it is later.
-- src:368 | (b) the employer of the Indian elects, by completing the form authorized by the Minister for such purpose, that, from the date of filing the form with the Minister or such later date as the employer specifies in the form, the employment of each Indian employee of the employer whose employment is not excepted from pensionable employment by other than paragraph 6(2)(j.1) of the Act is pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 29.1(1)(b) (src:368)
GIVEN `the day the employer files the form with the Minister` IS A DATE
      `the later day the employer specifies in the form` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 29.1(1)(b) — the day the employer's election takes effect` `the day the employer files the form with the Minister` `the later day the employer specifies in the form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the later day the employer specifies in the form`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the employer files the form with the Minister`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF specified GREATER THAN `the day the employer files the form with the Minister`
        THEN specified
        ELSE `the day the employer files the form with the Minister`

-- 29.1 (1) Subject to (2), pensionable employment includes the employment of an Indian, as defined in the Indian
-- Act, in Canada in a year, to the extent the employment is excepted from pensionable employment solely pursuant to
-- paragraph 6(2)(j.1) of the Act if (a) the Indian is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act;
-- and (b) the employer of the Indian elects as above.
