      `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment solely pursuant to paragraph 6(2)(j.1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Indian is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer of the Indian has made the election referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29.1(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment of an Indian when the employer has elected` `the person is an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act` `the employment is in Canada in the year` `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment solely pursuant to paragraph 6(2)(j.1) of the Act` `the Indian is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` `the employer of the Indian has made the election referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
        `the person is an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act`
    AND `the employment is in Canada in the year`
    AND `the employment is excepted from pensionable employment solely pursuant to paragraph 6(2)(j.1) of the Act`
    AND `the Indian is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act`
    AND `the employer of the Indian has made the election referred to in paragraph (1)(b)`

