§§ `Regulation 34: placement and employment agencies`

-- 34 (2) placement or employment agency includes any person or organization that is engaged in the business of
-- placing individuals in employment or for performance of services or of securing employment for individuals for a
-- fee, reward or other remuneration. "includes" leaves the ordinary meaning open: a case outside the clause
-- answers NOTHING.
-- src:382 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), placement or employment agency includes any person or organization that is engaged in the business of placing individuals in employment or for performance of services or of securing employment for individuals for a fee, reward or other remuneration.
@ref Reg 34(2) (src:382)
GIVEN `the person or organization is engaged in the business of placing individuals in employment or for performance of services, or of securing employment for individuals, for a fee, reward or other remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(2) — a person or organization is a placement or employment agency` `the person or organization is engaged in the business of placing individuals in employment or for performance of services, or of securing employment for individuals, for a fee, reward or other remuneration` MEANS
    IF `the person or organization is engaged in the business of placing individuals in employment or for performance of services, or of securing employment for individuals, for a fee, reward or other remuneration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 34 (1) Where any individual is placed by a placement or employment agency in employment with or for performance
-- of services for a client of the agency and the terms or conditions on which the employment or services are
-- performed and the remuneration is paid constitute a contract of service or are analogous to a contract of
-- service, the employment or performance of services is included in pensionable employment and the agency or the
-- client, whichever pays the remuneration to the individual, shall, for the purposes of maintaining records and
-- filing returns and paying, deducting and remitting contributions, be deemed to be the employer of the individual.
-- src:381 | 34 (1) Where any individual is placed by a placement or employment agency in employment with or for performance of services for a client of the agency and the terms or conditions on which the employment or services are performed and the remuneration thereof is paid constitute a contract of service or are analogous to a contract of service, the employment or performance of services is included in pensionable employment and the agency or the client, whichever pays the remuneration to the individual, shall, for the purposes of maintaining records and filing returns and paying, deducting and remitting contributions payable by and in respect of the individual under the Act and these Regulations, be deemed to be the employer of the individual.
@ref Reg 34(1) (src:381)
GIVEN `the individual is placed by a placement or employment agency in employment with or for performance of services for a client of the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms or conditions on which the employment or services are performed and the remuneration is paid constitute a contract of service or are analogous to a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 34(1) — the placed individual's employment is included in pensionable employment` `the individual is placed by a placement or employment agency in employment with or for performance of services for a client of the agency` `the terms or conditions on which the employment or services are performed and the remuneration is paid constitute a contract of service or are analogous to a contract of service` MEANS
    `the individual is placed by a placement or employment agency in employment with or for performance of services for a client of the agency`
    AND `the terms or conditions on which the employment or services are performed and the remuneration is paid constitute a contract of service or are analogous to a contract of service`

-- src:381 | 34 (1) Where any individual is placed by a placement or employment agency in employment with or for performance of services for a client of the agency and the terms or conditions on which the employment or services are performed and the remuneration thereof is paid constitute a contract of service or are analogous to a contract of service, the employment or performance of services is included in pensionable employment and the agency or the client, whichever pays the remuneration to the individual, shall, for the purposes of maintaining records and filing returns and paying, deducting and remitting contributions payable by and in respect of the individual under the Act and these Regulations, be deemed to be the employer of the individual.
@ref Reg 34(1) (src:381)
DECLARE `cr1 Party deemed to be the employer of a placed individual` IS ONE OF
    `the placement or employment agency`
    `the client of the placement or employment agency`

-- "whichever pays the remuneration": if both or neither pay it the text does not say (NOTHING).
@ref Reg 34(1) (src:381)
GIVEN `the employment is included in pensionable employment under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agency pays the remuneration to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the client pays the remuneration to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `cr1 Party deemed to be the employer of a placed individual`
`reg 34(1) — the party deemed to be the employer of the placed individual` `the employment is included in pensionable employment under subsection (1)` `the agency pays the remuneration to the individual` `the client pays the remuneration to the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the employment is included in pensionable employment under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the agency pays the remuneration to the individual` AND (NOT `the client pays the remuneration to the individual`) THEN JUST `the placement or employment agency`
        IF `the client pays the remuneration to the individual` AND (NOT `the agency pays the remuneration to the individual`) THEN JUST `the client of the placement or employment agency`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 34.1: international social security agreements`

-- 34.1 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Part (a) subject to paragraphs 6(2)(a) to (i), (j.1) and (k) of
-- the Act, if by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the
-- Act the legislation of Canada applies to a person in any year, the employment of that person in those
-- circumstances is included in pensionable employment for that year, if (i) the employer is an employer operating
-- in Canada within the meaning of subsection 15(1), (ii) the employer has, in respect of that employment, given an
-- undertaking in prescribed form to pay the employee's contributions and the employer's contributions under
-- sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II, or (iii) in
-- any case where the employer is not an employer operating in Canada and has not given the undertaking described
-- in (ii) or has not complied with the undertaking in the year, that person complies with the requirements of
-- paragraphs 29(c) to (f) in respect of that year; and (b) where by virtue of the circumstances described in an
-- agreement the legislation of the other country that is a party to the agreement applies to a person in any year,
-- the employment of that person in those circumstances is excepted from pensionable employment for that year.
-- (3) legislation has the meaning assigned to that term by the applicable agreement (an input here: the
-- agreements are not deposited).
-- src:383 | 34.1 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Part
-- src:384 | (a) subject to paragraphs 6(2)(a) to (i), (j.1) and (k) of the Act, if by virtue of any of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act the legislation of Canada applies to a person in any year, the employment of that person in those circumstances is included in pensionable employment for that year, if
-- src:385 | (i) his employer is an employer operating in Canada within the meaning given to that term by subsection 15(1),
-- src:386 | (ii) his employer has, in respect of that employment, given an undertaking in prescribed form to pay the employee’s contributions and the employer’s contributions under sections 8 and 9 respectively, of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II, or
-- src:387 | (iii) in any case where his employer is not an employer operating in Canada and has not given the undertaking described in subparagraph (ii) or has not complied with the undertaking in the year, that person complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f) in respect of that year; and
-- src:388 | (b) where by virtue of any of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act the legislation of the other country that is a party to the agreement applies to a person in any year, the employment of that person in those circumstances is excepted from pensionable employment for that year.
@ref Reg 34.1(1)(a) (src:383-387)
GIVEN `the legislation of Canada applies to the person in the year by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is excepted by paragraph 6(2)(a) to (i), (j.1) or (k) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has complied with the undertaking in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f) in respect of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 34.1(1)(a) — pensionable employment includes the employment under an agreement when the legislation of Canada applies` `the legislation of Canada applies to the person in the year by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act` `the employment is excepted by paragraph 6(2)(a) to (i), (j.1) or (k) of the Act` `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II` `the employer has complied with the undertaking in the year` `the person complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f) in respect of the year` MEANS
        `the legislation of Canada applies to the person in the year by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act`
    AND (NOT `the employment is excepted by paragraph 6(2)(a) to (i), (j.1) or (k) of the Act`)
    AND (    `the employer is an employer operating in Canada`
         OR  `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II`
         OR  (    (NOT `the employer is an employer operating in Canada`)
              AND (    (NOT `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II`)
                   OR (NOT `the employer has complied with the undertaking in the year`))
              AND `the person complies with the requirements of paragraphs 29(c) to (f) in respect of the year`))

@ref Reg 34.1(1)(b) (src:388)
GIVEN `the legislation of the other country that is a party to the agreement applies to the person in the year by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 34.1(1)(b) — the employment under an agreement is excepted when the legislation of the other country applies` `the legislation of the other country that is a party to the agreement applies to the person in the year by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act` MEANS
    `the legislation of the other country that is a party to the agreement applies to the person in the year by virtue of the circumstances described in an agreement entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act`

-- 34.1 (2) Paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply in respect of the employment of a person in employment that
-- is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subparagraph (1)(a)(ii).
-- src:389 | (2) Paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply in respect of the employment of a person in employment that is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subparagraph (1)(a)(ii).
@ref Reg 34.1(2) (src:389)
GIVEN `the employment is included in pensionable employment under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 34.1(2) — paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply to the employment included by virtue of the undertaking` `the employment is included in pensionable employment under paragraph (1)(a)` `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II` MEANS
    `the employment is included in pensionable employment under paragraph (1)(a)` AND `the employer has given an undertaking in a form the Minister has authorized to pay the contributions under sections 8 and 9 of the Act for the year and to file information returns in accordance with Part II`
